.TH GIT-@-WORK 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@-work \- Create work branches following Conventional Commits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @ work
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fITYPE\fR [\fIDESCRIPTION\fR]
.br
.B git @ work
\fB--name\fR \fIFULL-BRANCH-NAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBwork\fR command creates a new work branch for development following Conventional Commits specification. It helps organize your development workflow by creating branches with consistent naming conventions.
.PP
When creating hotfix branches, the command automatically switches to the trunk branch first to ensure the hotfix is based on the latest stable code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -n, --name
Specify the full branch name directly
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B TYPE
The type of work (required unless using --name). Valid types include:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfeature\fR - New features
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbugfix\fR - Bug fixes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhotfix\fR - Critical bug fixes (creates from trunk)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrelease\fR - Release preparation
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchore\fR - Maintenance tasks
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdocs\fR - Documentation updates
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstyle\fR - Code style changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrefactor\fR - Code refactoring
.IP \(bu 2
\fBperf\fR - Performance improvements
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtest\fR - Test additions/changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBci\fR - CI/CD changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbuild\fR - Build system changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrevert\fR - Revert commits
.RE
.TP
.B DESCRIPTION
Description of the work (optional, will prompt if not provided). The description will be formatted into kebab-case for the branch name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a feature branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ work feature add-user-authentication
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a bugfix branch with custom name:
.RS
.nf
git @ work --name bugfix/fix-login-validation
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a hotfix branch (will prompt for description):
.RS
.nf
git @ work hotfix
.fi
.RE
.SH WORKFLOW
.PP
1. Creates a new branch from current branch (or trunk for hotfix)
.br
2. Switches to the new branch
.br
3. Sets it as the working branch
.br
4. Provides next steps for your workflow
.PP
If there are uncommitted changes, the command will prompt to save them to WIP before creating the branch.
.SH SPECIAL CASES
.TP
.B Hotfix branches
Automatically switch to trunk branch first
.TP
.B Uncommitted changes
Will prompt to save to WIP before creating branch
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BR git-@ (1),
.BR git-@-sprout (1),
.BR git-@-hotfix (1)